related via the equation of state of the gas phase. The "reinsertion" move removes a randomly selected molecule and reinserts it at a random position. For rigid molecules, it uses orientational biasing, and for chains, the molecule is fully regrown (the internal configuration is modified). To properly sample the internal structure (i.e., bond/bend/torsions), the "partial reinsertion" move is useful. Several atoms of the molecule are kept fixed, while others are regrown. Because there is already space for the atoms, the acceptance ratios are high. The acceptance rule for full and partial regrowth is given by
